# Build context for apps/web/Dockerfile, which builds from the repository
# root (the app imports workspace packages from outside apps/web).
#
# Without this the context is ~600MB and, worse, the builder's `COPY . .`
# lands the *host's* node_modules and .venv on top of the ones installed
# inside the image — native binaries built for the wrong platform, and a
# build that fails in a way the Dockerfile itself does not explain.
# apps/api/.dockerignore covers the same ground for the API image, whose
# context is apps/api rather than the root.

.git/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Python — the API image installs its own from uv.lock.
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# Build output, regenerated inside the image.
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/.turbo/
**/.content-collections/
*.tsbuildinfo
apps/api/staticfiles/

# Local secrets must never reach a layer.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Not needed to build or run anything.
docs/
infra/
e2e/
**/e2e/
.github/
